      "id": 1,
      "text": "East Claridon is an unincorporated community in Claridon Township, Geauga County, Ohio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Claridon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits where U.S. Route 322 meets State Route 608, a crossroads that has guided travelers for generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Claridon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first permanent settlers arrived in 1829, laying the groundwork for a community that would thrive for centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Claridon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office has operated in East Claridon since 1828, making it one of Ohio’s oldest continuous postal sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Claridon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Locals pronounce the name as KLAIR‑ih‑duhn, a distinctive sound that echoes the town’s heritage.",
